      "id": "figure-2-p005",
      "label": "Figure 2",
      "kind": "figure",
      "number": "2",
      "page": 5,
      "caption": "Limitations of TGNs. [Left] Temporal graph with nodes u, v that TGN-Att/TGAT cannot distinguish. Colors are node features, edge features are identical, and t3 > t2 > t1. [Center] TCTs of u and v are non-isomorphic. However, the attention layers of TGAT/TGN-Att compute weighted averages over a same multiset of values, returning identical messages for u and v. [Right] MP-TGNs fail to distinguish the events (u, v, t3) and (v, z, t3) as TCTs of z and u are isomorphic. Meanwhile, CAW cannot separate (u, z, t3) and (u0, z, t3): the 3-depth TCTs of u and u0 are not isomorphic, but the temporal walks from u and u0 have length 1, keeping CAW from capturing structural differences.",
      "raw_text": "Figure 2: Limitations of TGNs. [Left] Temporal graph with nodes u, v that TGN-Att/TGAT cannot distinguish. Colors are node features, edge features are identical, and t3 > t2 > t1. [Center] TCTs of u and v are non-isomorphic. However, the attention layers of TGAT/TGN-Att compute weighted averages over a same multiset of values, returning identical messages for u and v. [Right] MP-TGNs fail to distinguish the events (u, v, t3) and (v, z, t3) as TCTs of z and u are isomorphic. Meanwhile, CAW cannot separate (u, z, t3) and (u0, z, t3): the 3-depth TCTs of u and u0 are not isomorphic, but the temporal walks from u and u0 have length 1, keeping CAW from capturing structural differences.",
